ink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/one-of-italys-most-popular-attractions-the-uffizi-galleries-in-florence-reveals-plans-for-a-major-renovation-over-the-next-two-years-180989295/</guid></item><item><title>在现代人类 DNA 中发现了两个已灭绝“幽灵”祖先的痕迹，暗示着我们极其复杂的家谱</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/traces-of-two-extinct-ghost-ancestors-were-found-hiding-in-modern-human-dna-hinting-at-our-extremely-complex-family-tree-180989250/</link><description>研究人员使用了一种新方法来研究过去与智人的杂交，这种方法不需要古代 DNA。该技术鉴定了现存人类基因组中来自未知古人类的区域，其中包括来自 180 万年前血统的基因组</description><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 15:34:44 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/traces-of-two-extinct-ghost-ancestors-were-found-hiding-in-modern-human-dna-hinting-at-our-extremely-complex-family-tree-180989250/</guid></item><item><title>首先是火山喷发，现在是甲壳类动物入侵？观看巨型龙虾占领庞贝古城</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/first-a-volcanic-eruption-now-a-crustacean-invasion-see-the-giant-lobsters-taking-over-the-ancient-city-of-pompeii-180989275/</link><description>波普艺术装置展出了艺术家菲利普·科尔伯特 (Philip Colbert) 的 30 多件雕塑，这是三十年来首次登陆庞贝的当代雕塑展</description><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 14:17:49 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/first-a-volcanic-eruption-now-a-crustacean-invasion-see-the-giant-lobsters-taking-over-the-ancient-city-of-pompeii-180989275/</guid></item><item><title>一项研究表明，世界各地的蝴蝶正在迁往新的栖息地，很大程度上是由于气候变化</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/butterflies-around-the-world-are-moving-to-new-habitats-largely-because-of-climate-change-a-study-suggests-180989279/</link><description>研究人员检查了来自 105 个国家的 1,758 种蝴蝶（约占所有已知蝴蝶种类的百分之十）的数据，估计全球大约十分之一的物种已经改变了其分布范围</description><pubDate>Fri, 07 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/butterflies-around-the-world-are-moving-to-new-habitats-largely-because-of-climate-change-a-study-suggests-180989279/</guid></item><item><title>南极血瀑布为何会喷出宝石红色的水？微生物提供了有关地质特征古代起源的新线索</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-does-antarcticas-blood-falls-spew-ruby-red-water-microbes-offer-new-clues-about-the-geologic-features-ancient-origins-180989271/</link><description>瀑布含有富含铁的盐水，当暴露在空气中时会氧化并变成红色。一项新的研究提供了进一步的证据，表明盐水可能来自数百万年前洪水退去时滞留的海水</description><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 20:26:01 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/why-does-antarcticas-blood-falls-spew-ruby-red-water-microbes-offer-new-clues-about-the-geologic-features-ancient-origins-180989271/</guid></item><item><title>在罗马斗兽场附近发现的这幅海洋生物马赛克提供了令人惊讶的线索——它的建筑可能是古罗马消防员的住所</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-marine-life-mosaic-discovered-near-the-colosseum-offers-a-surprising-clue-its-building-may-have-housed-firefighters-in-ancient-rome-180989273/</link><description>在公元二世纪建造这座建筑时，消防在古罗马已经是一个正式的职业</description><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 19:51:22 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-marine-life-mosaic-discovered-near-the-colosseum-offers-a-surprising-clue-its-building-may-have-housed-firefighters-in-ancient-rome-180989273/</guid></item><item><title>查尔斯·达尔文 (Charles Darwin) 推测这些植物在 150 年前是肉食性的。一项新研究证明他是对的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/charles-darwin-theorized-that-these-plants-were-carnivorous-150-years-ago-a-new-study-proves-him-right-180989265/</link><description>正如博物学家 1875 年预测的那样，一些虎耳草植物会捕食昆虫——利用粘性毛发来捕获昆虫</description><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 19:15:21 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/charles-darwin-theorized-that-these-plants-were-carnivorous-150-years-ago-a-new-study-proves-him-right-180989265/</guid></item><item><title>臭名昭著的野猫，以三年狩猎后捕获的稀有新西兰鸭子为食</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nine-lives-a-feral-cat-hunting-rare-ducks-in-new-zealand-has-been-caught-and-killed-after-three-years-180989267/</link><description>灰虎斑猫被称为“九命”，因为它多次逃脱捕获，它破坏了自然资源