ls-when-ships-are-near-highlighting-the-implications-of-underwater-noise-pollution-180989257/</guid></item><item><title>这艘因击沉敌舰而闻名的二战潜艇刚刚穿越密歇根湖进行了数百万美元的改造</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-world-war-ii-submaring-noted-for-its-success-sinking-enemy-ships-just-journeyed-across-lake-michigan-for-a-multimillion-dollar-makeover-180989269/</link><description>“银边”号航空母舰因其在太平洋的巡逻工作而赢得了十几颗战斗星。加托级潜艇现在是密歇根州博物馆的明星</description><pubDate>Thu, 06 Aug 2026 14:48:16 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-world-war-ii-submaring-noted-for-its-success-sinking-enemy-ships-just-journeyed-across-lake-michigan-for-a-multimillion-dollar-makeover-180989269/</guid></item><item><title>AI 走进歌剧院，为瓦格纳《指环》的周年纪念演出制作图像</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ai-went-to-the-opera-projecting-images-for-an-anniversary-production-of-wagners-ring-cycle-at-the-theater-where-he-first-staged-the-masterpiece-180989270/</link><description>理查德·瓦格纳花了四分之一个世纪才完成这部四部分歌剧。新作品名为“10010110”，利用生成人工智能来探索艺术品的演变</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 21:03:01 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/ai-went-to-the-opera-projecting-images-for-an-anniversary-production-of-wagners-ring-cycle-at-the-theater-where-he-first-staged-the-masterpiece-180989270/</guid></item><item><title>海王星可能曾经见证过一场月球大屠杀，将其原来的卫星“翻了个底朝天”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/neptune-may-have-once-witnessed-a-lunar-massacre-that-turned-its-original-moons-inside-out-180989266/</link><description>一项新的研究在地球的两颗内卫星中发现了一种意想不到的矿物，指出了毁灭性的过去，其中一个大型物体被拉入该系统并摧毁了以前较大的卫星</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 20:51:47 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/neptune-may-have-once-witnessed-a-lunar-massacre-that-turned-its-original-moons-inside-out-180989266/</guid></item><item><title>受本杰明·富兰克林“加入或死亡”号召团结的启发，一座蛇形雕塑正在费城逐段成形</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-serpentine-sculpture-inspired-by-benjamin-franklins-join-or-die-call-for-unity-is-taking-shape-segment-by-segment-in-philadelphia-180989263/</link><description>这件 46 英尺长的花岗岩艺术品由约翰·柯林斯 (John Collins) 创作，灵感源自 18 世纪的政治漫画，预计将于今年秋天在独立广场 (Independence Mall) 揭幕</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 14:16:18 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-serpentine-sculpture-inspired-by-benjamin-franklins-join-or-die-call-for-unity-is-taking-shape-segment-by-segment-in-philadelphia-180989263/</guid></item><item><title>食肉“超级蠕虫”可能成为博物馆和研究标本的新骨骼清洁人员</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/flesh-eating-superworms-could-become-a-new-skeleton-cleaning-crew-for-museum-and-research-specimens-180989258/</link><description>一项新的研究暗示，这些生物将是一种很好的替代方法，可以替代用于从骨头上去除肉的传统方法，包括皮甲虫、化学处理和煮沸，这些方法可能会造成损害或耗时</description><pubDate>Wed, 05 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/flesh-eating-superworms-could-become-a-new-skeleton-cleaning-crew-for-museum-and-research-specimens-180989258/</guid></item><item><title>这位美国飞行员在二战期间击落了 40 架敌机。研究人员在太平洋丛林中发现了他的飞机残骸，并将机翼带回了他的家乡</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-american-pilot-downed-4o-enemy-aircraft-during-world-war-ii-researchers-discovered-the-wreck-of-his-plane-in-a-pacific-jungle-and-brought-a-wing-back-to-his-home-state-180989259/</link><description>理查德·奉邦 (Richard I. Bong) 驾驶着一架装饰着他未来妻子玛姬 (Marge) 肖像的飞机，成为美国得分最高的“王牌”，并获得了荣誉勋章</description><pubDate>Tue, 04 Aug 2026 20:33:07 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-american-pilot-downed-4o-enemy-aircraft-during-world-war-ii-researchers-discovered-the-wreck-of-his-plane-in-a-pacific-jungle-and-brought-a-wing-back-to-his-home-state-180989259/</guid></item><item><title>两人感染环孢子虫病后死亡，这是与持续的多州疫情相关的首例已知死亡事件</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/two-peope-died-after-getting-sick-with-cyclosporiasis-marking-the-first-known-deaths